This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent**
   - **Project and branch.**
     - Canon-locking for "My Rival's Distance: The Lords of Cian" (author Abad Morel).
     - Repo: /home/user/Lords-of-Cian-Knowledge-Core, branch claude/new-session-yz7gdp.
     - Push with `git push -u origin claude/new-session-yz7gdp`.
     - Commit messages end with:
       ```
       Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
       Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U8ueiqG5KTWVijTkfiM5ie
       ```
   - **The three non-negotiable rules (CLAUDE.md).**
     1. Draft, present the full text, get Abad's explicit approval, then lock. The approval is quoted verbatim.
     2. The Series Launch Protocol gate.
     3. The Connective-Tissue Gate:
        - `python3 scripts/connective_tissue_check.py <draft>` exits 0 (mark proposed IDs as `**ID**`);
        - a fresh independent reviewer returns CLEAN ("if not, it NEVER passes");
        - propagation happens in the same batch;
        - presentation carries a connective-tissue note.
   - **Standing conventions.**
     - No AI attribution.
     - Child-safety hard stop: nothing sexual involving minors; Ashkeel stays adult-only and non-explicit, with an age-30 floor.
     - No PRs unless asked.
     - Keep the working tree clean (the Stop hook requires commit and push).
   - **Abad's most recent message:** "lock it, approve the picks, confirm all three". It approves:
     - VB-068 and the account craft standard (done, Batch 376);
     - the recommended name picks, which lock as their own rules;
     - the three rulings: greetings by action (R0.2); Spanish as spoken phrase only (M1); comic registers broader than VB-004 in told accounts, "drafted and locked as a VB-004 amendment".
   - **Earlier:** "lock it. once you're done we will move on to pyro and the Triad".

2. **Key Technical Concepts**
   - **Ledger:** canon-ledger.json, now version 37.8, 2,696 rules, last batch 376.
   - **VB-066/067** (series names, account types) and **VB-068** (account craft standard) are locked.
   - **LEX- prefix:** new, for in-world common vocabulary and venue names, one rule per name (VB-068 requires this).
   - **"Told account":** a Comrade Account, an Adversary Account, a Hearsay entry, or any scene in which a character tells a story aloud.
   - **Comic registers under the amendment:**
     - Each register VB-068 names counts in full: R0.4, R15, R18, M1, M2's funny boast, M3's parting jab, M4, M7, M9, and the comic stories of M6 and M11.
     - Any other talk counts only where its purpose in the telling is laughter.
   - **Background agents.**
     - Reviewers are read-only and fresh-context.
     - Fix agent ae6d93dd02f9754eb is resumed via SendMessage for each round of Pyro/Triad fixes.
   - **Dry-run pattern:** copy canon-ledger.json, CLAUDE.md, the merge script, the standard, lauris-letitia.md and the drafts into the scratchpad `dry/` directory, then run the merge with approval "test".

3. **Files and Code Sections**
   - **canon-ledger.json** — Batch 376 added VB-068 (category voice-bible), version 37.8.
   - **merge_batch376_vb068_account_craft.py** — run. It extracts the VB-068 text from the names-and-rule draft and strips backticks. APPROVAL = "lock it, approve the picks, confirm all three".
   - **docs/lords-of-cian/voice/account-craft-standard.md**
     - Header is now "Locked standard, approved by Abad 2026-10-04 and bound by `VB-068` (Batch 376)".
     - R0.2 and the M1 Spanish line are marked confirmed.
     - The comic-register lines say they wait for the VB-004 amendment.
     - Batch 377's merge will rewrite these further.
   - **docs/lords-of-cian/drafts/2026-10-04-account-craft-names-and-rule.md**
     - VB-068 is resolved and the approval quote filled in.
     - Part (c), items 4 and 5, are marked "Confirmed by Abad"; item 8 is marked as ruled yes.
   - **docs/lords-of-cian/drafts/2026-10-04-vb004-amendment-and-lex-names.md** (revision 14, unlocked; committed after the restart, "Draft revision 14")
     - (a) The VB-004 amendment, beginning "Amended Batch 377, 2026-10-04: In a told account, characters' talk may use comic registers broader than irony and understatement..." It contains:
       - the "told account" definition, and "For this amendment only, the teller's voice... counts as characters' talk; its reliability stays as `VB-067` sets it";
       - "Each register `VB-068` names is a comic register as ruled, in full: R0.4 (in the homage World, signifying, ritual insult, call and response, and the toast; on Cian, dock, forge, and Maw idiom carrying any of these), R15, R18, M1, M2's funny boast, M3's parting jab, M4, M7, M9, and the comic stories of M6 and M11. Any other talk the standard sets out is a comic register only where its purpose in the telling is laughter...";
       - the R0.4 toast defined as a long rhymed narrative of a badman's or trickster's exploits, apart from M8's closing drink toast;
       - outside a told account, irony and understatement still hold;
       - no change to narration or Dossier text;
       - narrators keep their own sheets (VB-021 to VB-025); track rulings (VB-020, 022, 024, 063, 064, 065, CC-034) and VB-030 still govern diction; Onyx stays under VB-063 alone;
       - the Comrade bound clause, the 50% rule, the phatic bar, fact over emotion, banned words and hard constraints;
       - the child-safety line, and "No character under thirty appears in or near any Ashkeel setting, and no sexual detail reaches the page there".
     - (a2) The VB-068 amendment: "...It reads the ruling's 'including' as it stands: in a told account, each register this rule names may run broad in full, and any other talk the account craft standard sets out may run broad where its purpose in the telling is laughter, within `VB-004` as amended."
     - (b) LEX-001 to LEX-025:
       - mainline: tapstead, the Slack Hawser, the Tallow Lamp, the Last Bell, the Call Yard, the Trough, the Sweat, a hewer, a bell, dice-house, the lykewake, the posted bill, the pump/pump-lads, a whistler;
       - homage World: the Shekere, kibanda, kinyozi, egbe, oju, pembe, kete, ulli, baraza, ayie — each with "Used in the homage World only (`MCD-313`), under `PH2-034`'s naming convention.";
       - Ashkeel: brazier-house (LEX-025).
       - LEX-002, 003, 004 and 015 carry "Its trade, custom, or offices are drafted as their own rule (`VB-068`)."
       - Held: N10b, and the RULE NEEDED keys N6, N7, N13, N16, H5, H6, H7.
     - (c) The propagation list, including the M2 "Gaps:" heading becoming "Street words:" and a pointer to the diff file.
     - (d) The connective-tissue note with flagged readings and a "For Abad to confirm" paragraph: named items count in full, which goes beyond item 8 (including M4's hazing and M7's teasing-in); purpose-test reach covers M8's comic arc, M10's tall tales, Cian corner ritual insult, the heckled brag and M5 jeering; he can name exclusions.
   - **docs/lords-of-cian/drafts/2026-10-04-batch377-propagation-full-text.diff**
     - The full before/after text of what the merge writes to the standard, the Lauris profile, the naming table and CLAUDE.md.
     - Regenerated from the dry run; "test" is replaced with "<approval quote, verbatim>".
   - **merge_batch377_vb004_amendment_lex_names.py** (not run). It:
     - parses the amendment with `re.search(r'\n"(Amended Batch 377, 2026-10-04:.+?)"\n', ...)` and LEX rules with `\*\*(LEX-\d{3})\*\*\. (.+?)(?=\n\n)`;
     - cleans text with `clean()` (joins hyphen line breaks, strips backticks and `**`);
     - assigns categories lexicon-mainline, lexicon-homage-world and lexicon-ashkeel;
     - appends to VB-004: amend + " Abad's ruling at VB-068's lock: 'lock it, approve the picks, confirm all three'; approval of this text: '{APPROVAL}'.";
     - reads the VB-068 amendment from the draft and appends " Abad's approval: '{APPROVAL}'.";
     - records rules_affected 27, version "37.9";
     - applies the REPL list to the standard (N12 lines, "(proposed)", the section 1 list, R0.4, R15, R18, M1, M4, M7 twice, M9, section 6, the item 17 addition, the M7 dock line, M2 street words), the regenerated item-14 block, removal of the R0.4 ruling note, and the NAMES map;
     - asserts that no NAME NEEDED marker remains for any locked key;
     - edits the Lauris profile's Pillar 3 line, the naming-table header (including the two departures and "Part (c), item 8 is resolved"), CLAUDE.md's prefix list (adds `LEX`) and the Batch 377 history paragraph after "Ledger at `ledger_version` 37.8, 2,696 rules, 376 batches.";
     - CLAUDE.md's history paragraph includes a sync-owed note for the read-only Voice Bible mirror.
     - Usage: `python3 merge_batch377_vb004_amendment_lex_names.py docs/lords-of-cian/drafts/2026-10-04-vb004-amendment-and-lex-names.md "<approval>"`.
   - **docs/lords-of-cian/character-profiles/pyro.md and triad-guardians.md**
     - Section 2 is proposed, with Status "profile in discussion (Section 2 proposed)"; the tracker rows in chronicle-tracks-status.md are updated.
     - Proposed Pyro content: A1-A4, B2 (birth order and the consent options a/b/c), B3/TB1 (identical), B6 (no recommendation), B12, B16 (no recommendation), the Kindlings, the close-third narrator, and the kill register.
     - Proposed Triad content: TA1-TA3, TB2 (no recommendation), TB9 (Engine front, new fact), TB10 (rename T.D.K.'s Coursers asset), the Tendings (the Keepings as alternative), objective third person (needs a VB ruling), and the kill register.
     - Seven review rounds are applied; the last commit is "Pyro and Triad profiles: seventh-review fixes applied", pushed.
   - **CLAUDE.md** — Batch 376 entry added. The Batch 377 entry will be added by the merge script.

4. **Errors and fixes**
   - **Script matching problems:**
     - Indentation mismatches (the M2 "Gaps:" block used 2 spaces, not 4) — fixed.
     - The Lauris profile match relied on a line break — fixed to the exact line.
     - The NAMES assert after the REPL had already consumed markers — changed to a final check that none remain.
     - The amendment regex broke after the header change — updated to the dated header.
   - **Review findings addressed across 14 LEX rounds:**
     - scope ambiguity, and a narration restriction Abad never ruled (removed: VB-004 governs dialogue only);
     - the child-safety line's scope, and the Ashkeel floor;
     - register-list fidelity (narrowing versus "including" taken whole, purpose-test decidability, the named list counting in full);
     - LEX-025's open flame (now a stone basin);
     - LEX-009's citation; LEX-012 lowercased; collision notes added (Breaker's Yard, quench troughs, Frequency Vaccine pumps);
     - "X, not Y" antitheses removed;
     - the VB-068 amendment text was missing from the draft (added as a2);
     - propagation gaps (section 6, item 17, M7, the Lauris profile, the CLAUDE.md history, the naming-table header);
     - hyphen-space artifacts in the ledger text;
     - the full propagation text now provided as a diff file.
   - **Pyro/Triad, seven rounds:**
     - a birth-order contradiction with MCD-022;
     - the Last Breakfast is a Book 1 beat, so the window ends at the Fulfillment Ceremony;
     - unlabeled new facts;
     - misstated option costs;
     - corrected entry lists for Kanja 290-314;
     - cross-file consistency;
     - "the Keepings" collides with Keeper names, so the Tendings is proposed;
     - B6 has no recommendation and carries its costs against the "most devastating blow" ranking and CC-161.
   - **Container restart** killed two reviews; both were relaunched. No work was lost, since everything had been committed.

5. **Problem Solving**
   - The register-scope question was settled by option (a): items VB-068 names count in full, and anything else uses the purpose test. It is flagged for Abad.
   - Approval-list dependencies are noted in the profiles: items 1, 2 and 38, and the Hask mortality question.

6. **All user messages**
   - "lock it, approve the picks, confirm all three" (the only user message in this segment).
   - Earlier context: "lock it. once you're done we will move on to pyro and the Triad".

7. **Pending Tasks**
   - The fourteenth independent review of the LEX/VB-004 draft is running (agent a34f33613299cadfd). If findings come back, fix them, regenerate the diff via dry run, commit, and re-review until CLEAN.
   - When CLEAN, present the VB-004 amendment, the VB-068 amendment, the LEX-001 to 025 text, the diff file and the connective-tissue note to Abad in full, with the flagged confirm points. On approval, run merge_batch377 with his verbatim quote, verify, commit and push.
   - Launch an eighth independent review of pyro.md and triad-guardians.md Section 2 (the seventh round's fixes are applied and pushed). Repeat until CLEAN, then present the (A) questions, profiles, B items and Game Plan candidates to Abad for collaborative ruling.
   - Later / owed:
